{
	"Name": "Okta - Modification Feed - Risk-Scored Modification Feed",
	"Description": "Alert: Alert - Okta - Modification Feed\nSchedule: every 15 minutes over the previous 15 minutes (edit the scheduled search to change it)\n\nEvery Okta configuration or account change (event types marked is_mod in okta_eventTypes, or ending in a modification verb such as .create, .update, .delete, .grant) whose risk score reaches Low priority (40) or above. This is a review feed rather than a detection: it is noisier than the other Okta alerts, and the alert keeps at most 50 events per run.\nOverall, the query enriches raw Okta System Log events, computes a risk score (modification profile), applies user/IP tuning (allow/deny), and emits a consistent alert title, priority, and context.\n\nInputs and dependencies:\nEvent source: Okta System Log (tag=$OKTA).\nPipeline stages (in query order) and the lookups they use:\n  - Extraction: Enumerated Value Extraction (EVX) of the System Log fields, including targets by type.\n  - Enrichment: Enumerated Value enrichment, normalization, and high priority user tuning control.\n      - okta_eventTypes: Maps eventType to category, subcategory, is_mod for risk categorization and alert naming scheme.\n      - okta_privileged_actor: Provides a tuning control for High Privileged Actor Accounts and weigh their severity/priority differently compared to an end user.\n      - okta_protected_target: Provides a tuning control for High Privileged Target Accounts and weigh their severity/priority differently compared to an end user.\n  - Risk score (modification profile): Performs risk calculations based on high priority user tuning control based on modification event types; uses the okta_privileged_actor and okta_protected_target weights from the enrichment stage.\n  - IP tuning: Provides a tuning control for IP addresses causing noisy false positives and true negatives.\n    - okta_ip_allowlist.csv: Provides a tuning control to suppress alerts from known-good IPs (resolved from clientIp, else requestIp), per alert or globally, with expiry.\n    - okta_ip_denylist.csv: Provides a tuning control to force-include or escalate alerts from watchlisted IPs (resolved from clientIp, else requestIp), per alert or globally, with expiry.\n  - User tuning: Provides a tuning control for end users causing noisy false positives and true negatives.\n    - okta_user_allowlist.csv: Provides a tuning control to suppress known-benign alerts for specific users (actor or target), either for a single alert name or globally, with expiry.\n    - okta_user_denylist.csv: Provides a tuning control to force-include or escalate alerts for specific users, optionally only when risk_score >= min_risk, per alert or globally.\n  - Alert fields: Normalized alert output (e.g. _alert_title, _alert_priority, and context)\n\nReference(s):\n  - Okta \n    - https://developer.okta.com/docs/reference/api/event-types/\n    - https://developer.okta.com/docs/api/openapi/okta-management/management/tag/SystemLog/\n  - Sigma:\n    - https://detection.fyi/sigmahq/sigma/identity/okta/?query=okta\n    - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/tree/master/rules/identity/okta\n  - Elastic:\n    - https://detection.fyi/elastic/detection-rules/integrations/okta/?query=okta\n    - https://github.com/elastic/detection-rules/tree/main/rules/integrations/okta",
	"Labels": [
		"okta",
		"modification-feed",
		"modification-feed"
	],
